# Finding C in Garnet 2.2.14 (RESULTS.md, "The three failures traced"); seed 115 of the second
# exploration. A kill of the replica g4 before step 22, a failover of shard 1 from g1 to g4, and a
# power cut before step 40. When g1 attaches to g4 as a replica it starts its AOF again at 1596
# and overwrites the bytes 1536 to 1595 of its file. After the power cut it replays the damaged
# file, stops at the damage without an error, and reports g4's offset: it lacks every write after
# the failover and holds an empty string for a counter.
# params: device=FileStream reest=5
# commands: anytime_read first_init parallel_driver_del parallel_driver_hset parallel_driver_incr parallel_driver_lua parallel_driver_over parallel_driver_rpush parallel_driver_sadd parallel_driver_set parallel_driver_setex parallel_driver_txn parallel_driver_zadd serial_driver_failover serial_driver_migrate serial_driver_save
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=cut dseed=0 | run K=g4@22+1 C=40 W=a0075364,p1,q1,r500
